window.QUESTIONS_2024S=[{"id":1,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Sound signals are digitized. Sampling is performed at Time 1 through Time 5 in the figure below, and four-level quantization is performed; in other words, the levels closest to the sampling point are selected. After that, two-bit encoding is performed. The result is “11 01 00 10 11”. When digitization is performed in the same way, which of the following figures represents the sound signal that results in “01 00 10 11 01”?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Amplitude0001101112345Time"},{"key":"B","text":"Amplitude0001101112345Time"},{"key":"C","text":"Amplitude0001101112345Time"},{"key":"D","text":"Amplitude0001101112345Time"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"Sampling records the signal amplitude only at the specified times. Four-level quantization then replaces each sampled amplitude with the nearest level, and the two-bit code for those five levels must therefore be 01, 00, 10, 11, 01 in that exact order. At Times 1 through 5, the nearest quantization levels are respectively 01, 00, 10, 11, and 01, exactly matching the required code sequence."},{"id":2,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the logical operation that is equivalent to the truth table below?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AND"},{"key":"B","text":"NOT"},{"key":"C","text":"OR"},{"key":"D","text":"XOR"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"An AND operation outputs 1 only when both inputs are 1. For every other combination, at least one input is 0, so the output is 0. The AND truth table is 0, 0, 0, 1 for inputs 00, 01, 10, and 11."},{"id":3,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a standard encoding system that is widely used for handling multilingual text and symbols around the world as a single character set?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ASCII"},{"key":"B","text":"EBCDIC"},{"key":"C","text":"EUC"},{"key":"D","text":"Unicode"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"Unicode assigns code points to characters from many writing systems and to symbols in one universal character repertoire. Encodings such as UTF-8 and UTF-16 are ways of representing those Unicode code points as bytes. Unicode is the standard designed to represent text and symbols from languages around the world in a unified character set."},{"id":4,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"When a chairperson and a secretary are selected from three (3) candidates with a method that allows dual roles, there are three (3) ways for the selection of a single chairperson and three (3) ways for the selection of a secretary, so in total, there are nine (9) combinations for the selection of a chairperson and a secretary. When a chairperson and a secretary are selected from five (5) candidates with a method that allows dual roles, how many combinations for the selection are there?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"25"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"Because dual roles are allowed, selecting the chairperson does not remove that person from consideration for secretary. There are 5 choices for each role, so the multiplication principle gives 5 × 5 = 25 ordered role assignments. With dual roles permitted, each of 5 chairperson choices can be paired with any of 5 secretary choices, giving 25."},{"id":5,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"The function calGrade receives the student’s score and returns the grade. The score is an integer. If the score is greater than or equal to 80, the function calGrade returns “A”; if the score is between 65 and 79, it returns “B”; between 50 and 64, it returns “C”; and otherwise, it returns “Fail.” Which of the following is an appropriate piece of code to be inserted in blank in the program?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"score ≥ 65"},{"key":"B","text":"score ≥ 65 or score ≤ 79"},{"key":"C","text":"score ≤ 65 and score ≥ 79"},{"key":"D","text":"score ≤ 79"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"The conditions are tested from top to bottom. Reaching the second condition already means score < 80, so testing score ≥ 65 is sufficient to select exactly the range 65 through 79. Combined with the failed score ≥ 80 test, score ≥ 65 identifies scores from 65 to 79."},{"id":6,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"The procedure described below is sequentially performed for two (2) variables x and y, starting with step (1). When the procedure is completed, what is the resulting value of x?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"8"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"Initially x = 2 and y = 3. The first loop changes y to 2 and x to 4; the second changes y to 1 and x to 5, after which the procedure stops. Two passes add 2 and then 1 to the initial x of 2, producing 5."},{"id":7,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"There exist four (4) states numbered 1 through 4. The four (4) states are connected as shown in the figure below, and the state transition occurs in a clockwise or counter-clockwise direction.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-06.png","explanation":"Starting at state 1, 1 × 11 leaves remainder 2 when divided by 3, so the first transition moves two states clockwise to state 3. Then 3 × 11 is divisible by 3, so the second transition moves one state clockwise from 3 to 4. The first transition is 1 to 3 and the second is 3 to 4."},{"id":8,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"There is a device that stacks products from the bottom to the top, and removes the products sequentially from the top. There are only two (2) operations for this device.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"B","text":"B, A, C"},{"key":"C","text":"C, A, B"},{"key":"D","text":"C, B, A"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-06.png","explanation":"The device is a stack, so it follows last-in, first-out order for items that remain stored. Push and pop operations may be interleaved with arrivals, but an item below another stored item cannot be removed first. To remove C first, A, B, and C must all have been pushed; after popping C, B is above A, so A cannot be removed before B."},{"id":9,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"The program performs circular left shifting on the array elements. For example, after circular left shifting, the initial array {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} becomes {2, 3, 4, 5, 1}. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of pieces of code to be inserted in A and B in the program?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"i + 1array[the number of elements of array - 1]"},{"key":"B","text":"i + 1array[the number of elements of array]"},{"key":"C","text":"i - 1array[the number of elements of array - 1]"},{"key":"D","text":"i - 1array[the number of elements of array]"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"For a left shift, each element at index i from 2 onward must be copied to the preceding index i − 1. The saved first element is then placed in the last array position to complete the circular shift. A = i − 1 moves every later element one position left, and B is the final array element where the original first value belongs."},{"id":10,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the unique value that is sequentially assigned to a memory location in order to identify the location of instructions or data stored in the main memory of a computer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Address"},{"key":"B","text":"Counter"},{"key":"C","text":"Index"},{"key":"D","text":"Pointer"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"Main memory is organized as identifiable locations. The unique number assigned to each location so that the processor can read or write instructions and data there is its memory address. An address uniquely identifies a memory location."},{"id":11,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of HDMI?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is an interface for an AV device that handles the input and output of video, audio, and control signals through a single cable."},{"key":"B","text":"It is an interface that makes use of the infrared rays used in the exchange of information between cell phones."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a serial interface that connects an external hard disk or such other devices through a cable."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a wireless interface that makes use of radio waves and can perform communication even when there is a slight shielding."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"HDMI stands for High-Definition Multimedia Interface. It carries digital video and audio, together with supported control information, through a single cable between audiovisual devices. This describes HDMI's combined digital audiovisual and control-signal interface."},{"id":12,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of GPU?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is an index that shows the throughput of a CPU in terms of how many billions of instructions it can execute per second."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a frequency signal that synchronizes the arithmetic processing of CPUs."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a storage unit that is placed between a CPU and a main memory, and has a higher reading and writing speed than the main memory."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a processing unit that is used instead of a CPU to accelerate processing such as image processing for 3D graphics."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"A GPU is a Graphics Processing Unit. Its highly parallel processing design accelerates graphics operations and can also accelerate other workloads suited to parallel computation. A GPU is a processing unit used to accelerate workloads such as 3D image processing."},{"id":13,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"If a process from when a PC is powered on to when it becomes ready to use is divided into four (4) stages, which of the following is the stage that is performed first?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Loading a BIOS"},{"key":"B","text":"Loading an OS"},{"key":"C","text":"Loading resident application software such as antivirus software"},{"key":"D","text":"Loading device drivers"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"At power-on, the processor begins executing firmware startup code, commonly referred to here as the BIOS. That firmware initializes and checks hardware and then starts the process of loading the operating system, after which drivers and resident applications become available. BIOS firmware is the first of the listed stages involved in starting the PC."},{"id":14,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the reliability of a system or a device?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Controlling a system in a safe state in order to minimize damage when a fault occurs in a device is called foolproof."},{"key":"B","text":"Reducing the probability of occurrence of a fault in a device by using high-quality and high-reliability parts and elements is called fail-safe."},{"key":"C","text":"Enabling continuation of system processing when a fault occurs in a system due to an error is called fault tolerance."},{"key":"D","text":"Taking measures in the design stage so that humans do not make mistakes in system operation, or no faults or failures occur even if they make mistakes is called fail soft."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"Fault tolerance is the ability of a system to continue providing service when a component fault or error occurs, often by using redundancy or alternate processing. The other choices attach the wrong names to distinct reliability and safety concepts. Continuing system processing despite a fault is fault tolerance."},{"id":15,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Among the costs below concerning a sales management system, which of the following is the list that contains all costs that are included in TCO?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(i), (ii)"},{"key":"B","text":"(i), (iv)"},{"key":"C","text":"(ii), (iii)"},{"key":"D","text":"(iii), (iv)"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) includes the costs of acquiring, operating, supporting, and maintaining the information system over its life. Product purchasing and shipping are business transaction costs handled by the sales system, not ownership costs of that system. Both software maintenance and hardware maintenance are continuing costs of owning and operating the system."},{"id":16,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In a web service and other services, in order to increase reliability and process a large volume of accesses from users, which of the following is a technique that links multiple computers and makes them work as if they were a single computer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Clustering"},{"key":"B","text":"Spooling"},{"key":"C","text":"Buffering"},{"key":"D","text":"Mirroring"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"Clustering coordinates multiple computers so that they provide a service as one logical system. It can distribute workload for higher capacity and provide redundancy for improved availability. Clustering links multiple computers into one logical service to improve scalability and reliability."},{"id":17,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In a file system with the hierarchy structure shown in the Figure, when “..\\..\\DIRB\\Fn.txt” is specified from the directory marked with an * (the current directory), which of the following is the file that is referenced? Here, blank in the Figure show the directory name, and the reference method for a file is as below.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Fn.txt at (1)"},{"key":"B","text":"Fn.txt at (2)"},{"key":"C","text":"Fn.txt at (3)"},{"key":"D","text":"Fn.txt at (4)"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"The current directory is the innermost DIRB under Root\\DIRB\\DIRA. The first .. moves to DIRA, the second .. moves to Root\\DIRB, and then DIRB selects its child DIRB, so Fn.txt at position (4) is referenced. After two parent moves, DIRB\\Fn.txt resolves to the file marked (4)."},{"id":18,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning OSS (Open Source Software)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Use in industries that require high quality, such as the medical industry, is prohibited."},{"key":"B","text":"Various types of license exist, and the terms of license must be observed when the software is used."},{"key":"C","text":"If the source code is released on the Internet, the software can be called OSS even if redistribution is prohibited."},{"key":"D","text":"The software must not be sold for a fee."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"Open Source Software is distributed under an open-source license, and those licenses can impose different conditions on use, modification, notices, source distribution, or redistribution. Users and distributors must follow the terms of the particular license. Open-source licenses vary, and their applicable terms must be observed."},{"id":19,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a term that means the validation of a software license by using the product ID and the user’s hardware information, in order to prevent unauthorized use of the software?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Activation"},{"key":"B","text":"Cloud computing"},{"key":"C","text":"Streaming"},{"key":"D","text":"Fragmentation"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-11.png","explanation":"Product activation verifies that a software installation is authorized, often by checking a product key or ID together with installation or device information. Its purpose is to limit use that violates the software license. Activation is the license-validation process described."},{"id":20,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Sales data by month for each branch is evaluated. In the “Evaluation” field for each branch by month, if the amount of sales at the branch is below the average sales amount of branches A through C for the month, the symbol “X” is to be displayed, and if the amount is above or equal to the average, the symbol “O” is to be displayed. Which of the following is an appropriate expression to be entered in cell C3? Here, the expression that is entered in cell C3 is copied and used in cell D3, cell E3, cells C5 through E5, and cells C7 through E7.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IF($C2 < AVERAGE(C2 : E2) , 'O' , 'X')"},{"key":"B","text":"IF($C2 < AVERAGE(C2 : E2) , 'X' , 'O')"},{"key":"C","text":"IF(C2 < AVERAGE($C2 : $E2) , 'O' , 'X')"},{"key":"D","text":"IF(C2 < AVERAGE($C2 : $E2) , 'X' , 'O')"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-11.png","explanation":"The sales cell must change with the branch column, while the average range must always cover columns C through E for the same month row. Therefore C2 is relative, $C2:$E2 fixes only the range's columns, and the IF returns X when the branch value is below the average. C2 moves with the copied formula, $C2:$E2 keeps the three branch columns fixed, and the output symbols follow the stated rule."},{"id":21,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description about the function keys of a PC?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They are the keys where specific functions are assigned for each application and OS."},{"key":"B","text":"They display a keyboard shape on a screen and enable input processing with software."},{"key":"C","text":"They have a security role and are keys for performing encryption and decryption."},{"key":"D","text":"They are information to identify specific lines uniquely in a database."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"Function keys, typically labeled F1, F2, and so on, are keyboard keys whose actions are defined by the operating system or the active application. The same key can therefore perform different functions in different contexts. Function keys are assigned specific actions by an OS or application."},{"id":22,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a technology that is also used in measures against tampering of software in IoT devices and verifies the digital signature of the OS, firmware, or other such software when it is started, and only executes the software if the verification is successful?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"GPU"},{"key":"B","text":"RAID"},{"key":"C","text":"Secure boot"},{"key":"D","text":"Reboot"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"Secure boot establishes trust during startup by checking a digital signature before allowing firmware, a boot loader, an operating system, or other startup software to execute. Software whose signature cannot be validated is rejected, helping prevent unauthorized startup code. Secure boot verifies signed startup software and proceeds only when verification succeeds."},{"id":23,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning a smart meter that is an IoT device?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is embedded in a car navigation system or a game controller, and measures the extent of change in speed."},{"key":"B","text":"It is installed in a house or other such place and automatically measures consumption of electricity and gas, and sends the data to the supplier by using a cellular network, etc."},{"key":"C","text":"It deletes the data that is stored on a mobile terminal such as a smartphone or mobile PC from a remote location via a network."},{"key":"D","text":"In addition to counting the number of steps, it identifies the walking route, detects the walking speed and height variations in the route, and calculates the energy consumed."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"A smart meter automatically measures utility usage and communicates the readings to the utility provider. This supports remote meter reading and more detailed consumption management without a person visiting the site. Automatic electricity or gas measurement and network transmission are characteristic smart-meter functions."},{"id":24,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate reason for using a style sheet in the creation of a website?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The data between the web server and the web browser can be exchanged in a safe manner."},{"key":"B","text":"The users can be notified of update to the website."},{"key":"C","text":"The users of the website can be identified."},{"key":"D","text":"The appearance of multiple web pages can be easily unified."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"A style sheet, such as CSS, separates presentation rules from page content. Applying shared rules to many pages makes fonts, colors, spacing, and layout consistent and easier to maintain. A shared style sheet can unify the appearance of multiple web pages."},{"id":25,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"A technique that represents a figure with pixels is considered. In the case of Fig. 1, when each row of the figure of 3×3 pixels is read on a pixel-by-pixel basis from upper left to right and B and W are respectively written for black and white, the result is “BWBBBBBWB” (9 characters). Then, when a succession of n characters of “B”s or “W”s is represented as “Bn” or “Wn” respectively (where n is an integer of 2 or greater), Fig. 1 can be represented as “BWB5WB” (6 characters) and the compression ratio in this case is defined as 6/9 or 66.7%. When the figure of 5×5 pixels in Fig. 2 is represented by using the same technique, what is the compression ratio in percentage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"48.0"},{"key":"B","text":"52.0"},{"key":"C","text":"76.0"},{"key":"D","text":"88.0"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"Reading Fig. 2 continuously produces runs that encode to 13 characters: B6, W4, B4, W, B, W4, B, W4. The original has 25 pixels, so the compression ratio is 13 ÷ 25 × 100 = 52.0%. The encoded length is 13 characters and 13/25 equals 52.0%."},{"id":26,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"There are “Sales”, “Customer” and “Product” tables in a relational database. Among lists A through C, which of the following contains all and only the lists that can be created from the data in these tables? Here, a solid underlined part represents a primary key, and a dashed underlined column represents a foreign key.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C"},{"key":"D","text":"B, C"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"List A can be produced by joining Sales to Customer and totaling sales by customer for the chosen period. List C can be produced by joining Sales to Product and aggregating sales amounts by product. List B cannot be determined because no inventory or stock records are present. The available sales, customer, and product data are sufficient for A and C only."},{"id":27,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In the description below concerning the design process of a relational database, which of the following is an appropriate combination of terms to be inserted into blanks A through C?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"instancesE-R diagramfunctions"},{"key":"B","text":"instancesflowcharttables"},{"key":"C","text":"relationshipsE-R diagramtables"},{"key":"D","text":"relationshipsflowchartfunctions"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"Conceptual database design identifies entities and the relationships among them, commonly represented in an entity-relationship (E-R) diagram. That model is then used to design relational tables. Relationships complete the E-R diagram, which provides the basis for designing tables."},{"id":28,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate combination of relational database manipulations I through III and relational operations?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"JoinProjectionSelection"},{"key":"B","text":"ProjectionJoinSelection"},{"key":"C","text":"ProjectionSelectionJoin"},{"key":"D","text":"SelectionProjectionJoin"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"Projection chooses columns, selection chooses rows that satisfy a condition, and join combines related rows from two or more tables. These are distinct relational operations. I is projection, II is selection, and III is join."},{"id":29,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of commit in transaction processing?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a transaction attempts to update shared data, other transactions are blocked from updating this data."},{"key":"B","text":"The update is confirmed in the database. It is used when a transaction is processed normally."},{"key":"C","text":"The database is returned to the status prior to the start of a transaction. It is used when the transaction is not processed normally for some reason."},{"key":"D","text":"Multiple tables are made into one (1) table by using the columns as keys that relate the tables to each other."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"A commit completes a successful transaction by making its database changes permanent and visible according to the database's transaction rules. If processing cannot complete normally, a rollback is used instead to undo the transaction's changes. Commit confirms the updates made by a normally completed transaction."},{"id":30,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"When an e-mail is sent to multiple recipients, there are cases that no recipient of the e-mail should know the e-mail addresses of other recipients. In such cases, which of the following is an appropriate place where the e-mail addresses of the multiple recipients are entered?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Bcc"},{"key":"B","text":"Cc"},{"key":"C","text":"To"},{"key":"D","text":"Both To and Bcc"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"Addresses in the blind carbon copy (Bcc) field are hidden from the other recipients. This lets one message be sent to multiple people without disclosing the recipient list to them. Bcc conceals each listed recipient address from the other recipients."},{"id":31,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is not an appropriate description of online storage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It can be used not only from a computer, but also from a smartphone or a tablet, if the device is connected to the Internet."},{"key":"B","text":"There is a free service that can be used with limited capacity and functionalities."},{"key":"C","text":"There is a service that allows multiple registered users to share and edit the same file."},{"key":"D","text":"If the capacity of the auxiliary storage unit built into the user’s computer or tablet is increased, the capacity of online storage will also increase automatically."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"Online storage capacity is provided by a remote service and is governed by that service's plan and limits. Increasing a device's local auxiliary storage does not automatically change the amount of remote storage allocated to the account."},{"id":32,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an example of damage incurred by the theft of cookies by a cross-site scripting attack or other attack?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The PC becomes infected by a virus."},{"key":"B","text":"The files on the PC are sent to an outside destination."},{"key":"C","text":"Web service accounts are hijacked."},{"key":"D","text":"Intrusion into the network takes place over the wireless LAN."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"A cookie can contain a session identifier that tells a web service which authenticated session a request belongs to. If an attacker steals a usable session cookie, the attacker may impersonate the victim and take over the web account without knowing the password. A stolen session cookie can enable session hijacking and unauthorized use of a web service account."},{"id":33,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"When a web page with URL “http://srv01.itpec.org/abc.html” is accessed on the Internet, what does “srv01” in the URL stand for?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The fact that “itpec.org” is a web service"},{"key":"B","text":"The file name of the web page where an access is requested"},{"key":"C","text":"The fact that HTTP or HTTPS can be specified as a communication protocol"},{"key":"D","text":"The host name of a computer that belongs to the domain name “itpec.org”"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"In srv01.itpec.org, itpec.org is the domain and srv01 is the host label identifying a particular computer or service within that domain. The remaining abc.html component identifies the requested resource path. srv01 is the host name within the itpec.org domain."},{"id":34,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"A large number of IP addresses are required in order to connect a massive number of IoT devices to the Internet, so the decision was made to use the Internet Protocol with IP addresses that have a length of 128 bits. Which of the following is this protocol?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IPv4"},{"key":"B","text":"IPv5"},{"key":"C","text":"IPv6"},{"key":"D","text":"IPv8"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"IPv6 uses 128-bit IP addresses, providing a vastly larger address space than IPv4. This large address space supports the continuing growth of Internet-connected systems, including IoT devices. IPv6 defines 128-bit IP addresses."},{"id":35,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a definition of a zero-day attack that is a threat to information security?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It stops the target system of the attack within 24 hours from the start of the attack."},{"key":"B","text":"It causes the onset immediately after the infection by using a virus without an incubation period."},{"key":"C","text":"It exploits vulnerability before any countermeasure against the software vulnerability is made public."},{"key":"D","text":"It immediately obtains confidential information from a third party through social engineering or eavesdropping."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"A zero-day attack exploits a previously unknown vulnerability. Choice c describes the exam's focus on exploitation before a public countermeasure is available. Attacking a known flaw merely because an available patch has not been installed is not, by itself, a zero-day attack. It describes exploitation before a countermeasure for the vulnerability has been made public."},{"id":36,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate action for the secure use of a smartphone?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Using it without updating OS and using the same version of the OS as at the time of purchase"},{"key":"B","text":"Enhancing the functions by making alterations such as jailbreak"},{"key":"C","text":"Setting up a feature that locks the screen with a password"},{"key":"D","text":"Downloading applications that are considered to be useful from any web site"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"A screen lock protected by a password reduces unauthorized access if the smartphone is lost, stolen, or left unattended. Secure use also normally includes timely updates, avoiding unauthorized system modifications, and obtaining applications from trusted sources. A password-protected screen lock is a basic access-control measure."},{"id":37,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Security risk treatment in ISMS includes risk transfer, risk avoidance, risk acceptance, and risk reduction. Which of the following is an example of risk avoidance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A security measure was taken, which lowered the possibility of problems arising."},{"key":"B","text":"The company took out insurance in case a problem arises and causes damage."},{"key":"C","text":"The risk was confirmed to be small, and it was decided that damage would be borne by the company when a problem arises."},{"key":"D","text":"The company withdrew from the services that carried high risk."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"Risk avoidance removes the activity or condition that creates the risk, so the organization is no longer exposed to it. This differs from reducing likelihood, transferring financial impact, or knowingly accepting the risk. Withdrawing from the high-risk service removes the risk-producing activity and is risk avoidance."},{"id":38,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description of the beginning of a URL indicating that TLS is used for communication between a web browser and a web server?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"http://"},{"key":"B","text":"https://"},{"key":"C","text":"shttp://"},{"key":"D","text":"ssl://"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"HTTPS is HTTP carried over a TLS-protected connection. Therefore a web URL whose browser-server communication uses TLS begins with the https scheme. https:// identifies HTTP communication protected with TLS."},{"id":39,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a technique that is used to detect that the received data has been tampered with?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Compression"},{"key":"B","text":"Digital signature"},{"key":"C","text":"Password authentication"},{"key":"D","text":"Filtering"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"A digital signature is created from the signed data through cryptographic operations. Verification fails if the received data has changed, so a valid signature provides evidence of integrity as well as the origin associated with the signing key. Digital-signature verification can detect tampering with the signed data."},{"id":40,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Among I through III below, which of the following lists all and only the appropriate measures for preventing a PC from getting infected with viruses?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I"},{"key":"B","text":"I, II"},{"key":"C","text":"I, III"},{"key":"D","text":"II, III"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"Applying security patches closes known software vulnerabilities that malware may exploit. Security education helps users recognize malicious attachments, links, downloads, and other infection routes. Disk striping affects storage layout and performance, not virus prevention. Both patching software and educating users help prevent virus infection."},{"id":41,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate example of phishing?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"An attacker’s act of sending a command via network to a virus-infected PC and having it execute an illegal program"},{"key":"B","text":"Sending an e-mail that pretends to be from a financial institution, directing a user to a false web site, and acquiring a password"},{"key":"C","text":"Identifying a password by using a dictionary data that enumerates strings that are likely to be used as a password"},{"key":"D","text":"Sending a large number of packets from multiple computers to a target server and disabling the function of the server"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"Phishing impersonates a trusted organization or person to manipulate a victim into revealing credentials or other sensitive information. A common pattern is a deceptive message containing a link to a fake login page. The fake financial-institution email and website are used to steal a password, which is phishing."},{"id":42,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning behavioral detection technology for protecting systems from unknown threats such as zero-day attacks?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It detects that a PC has not been used for a certain period of time, darkens the screen automatically, and displays a changing image."},{"key":"B","text":"It suspends use of an account when it detects that an incorrect password is entered on a web site more than a set number of times."},{"key":"C","text":"It continually monitors the activity of programs and stops any program with any suspicious activity, such as unusual communication to an outside destination."},{"key":"D","text":"It changes users’ input on a web site into safe character strings when it detects any harmful character string that could cause malfunction."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"Behavioral detection looks for suspicious actions rather than relying only on a known-malware signature. Because it monitors what a program actually does, it may identify previously unknown threats when they communicate, modify data, or execute in unusual ways. Continuous monitoring and stopping programs that show suspicious activity is behavioral detection."},{"id":43,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is appropriate as the characteristic of single sign-on?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is an effective countermeasure for information leakage because data is processed and stored on a server side, and data does not remain on devices."},{"key":"B","text":"It implements high availability because when the data is saved, it is automatically distributed and stored on multiple disks."},{"key":"C","text":"It implements high confidentiality because it employs authentication that uses fingerprint and iris in addition to a password."},{"key":"D","text":"It implements high convenience because once a user is authenticated, he or she is allowed to use multiple services without any more authentication."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"Single sign-on (SSO) allows one authentication session to grant access to multiple connected services. Its primary characteristic in this question is user convenience because repeated login prompts are reduced. After one successful authentication, SSO permits access to multiple services without authenticating separately to each one."},{"id":44,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions from A through C, which of the following is the list that contains all and only appropriate features of VPN?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"A, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B"},{"key":"D","text":"C"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"A VPN creates a logically private, protected connection over a shared or public network, allowing remote users or sites to communicate as though connected to a private organizational network. Wireless peer-to-peer communication and endpoint security assessment are separate technologies. Only B correctly states that a public network can be used like a private company network through a VPN."},{"id":45,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"When an attacker makes an unauthorized intrusion into a computer, the attacker sometimes changes a program or settings in the computer in order to make further intrusions into the computer easier. Which of the following is the most appropriate term to express the method used by the attacker for further intrusions into the computer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Tapping"},{"key":"B","text":"Backdoor"},{"key":"C","text":"Phishing"},{"key":"D","text":"Port scan"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"A backdoor is a hidden or unauthorized means of bypassing normal access controls. An intruder may install or configure one after an initial compromise so that later access is easier. A persistent unauthorized entry mechanism created for later intrusion is a backdoor."},{"id":46,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In order to achieve a non-stop system, which of the following is an appropriate item to be considered during the design of the system architecture?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Partitioning of software into components"},{"key":"B","text":"Encryption of data"},{"key":"C","text":"Reduction in power consumption of hardware"},{"key":"D","text":"Dual redundancy of hardware"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"A non-stop system must continue operating even when a hardware component fails. Dual hardware redundancy provides a second component or system that can take over when the active one fails, reducing a single point of failure. Dual hardware redundancy supports continuous operation by providing an alternate when one unit fails."},{"id":47,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"A detailed design document of software is created as an output of software detailed design. Which of the following is the person who takes charge of the next process of development upon receipt of this output?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"System auditor"},{"key":"B","text":"System operator in-charge"},{"key":"C","text":"System user"},{"key":"D","text":"Programmer"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"Detailed software design translates higher-level design into specifications precise enough for coding. The next development process is implementation, in which a programmer uses the detailed design document to create the program. The programmer receives the detailed design and implements it in code."},{"id":48,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Mr. A, a developer, is analyzing and verifying the internal structure of a program in order to determine whether input data is processed as intended. Which of the following is the test that Mr. A is currently conducting?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"System test"},{"key":"B","text":"Top-down test"},{"key":"C","text":"Black box test"},{"key":"D","text":"White box test"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"White-box testing designs tests with knowledge of a program's internal code, control flow, conditions, and paths. Analyzing the internal structure to verify how input is processed is therefore white-box testing. Inspection of internal program structure and processing paths is white-box testing."},{"id":49,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through D concerning software installation, which of the following lists all and only the appropriate descriptions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, C"},{"key":"B","text":"B, C, D"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"D"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"Production installation should follow an implementation plan that has been reviewed and agreed before the change is made. Planning and approval cannot be postponed until after installation merely because of a deadline or because development was internal. D properly requires a plan and agreement before installing the added production function."},{"id":50,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate term expressing initiatives to improve the services where the development side and the operations side of the system cooperate to proactively automate operations of the system and transition to the new production system, and release new functions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"DevOps"},{"key":"B","text":"RAD"},{"key":"C","text":"Object-oriented development"},{"key":"D","text":"Test-driven development"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"DevOps promotes collaboration between software development and IT operations, supported by automation of building, testing, deployment, release, and operational work. The aim is to deliver service improvements and new functions reliably and frequently. The described cooperation and proactive automation are central DevOps practices."},{"id":51,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning project scope management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It defines and manages deliverables such as the products and services to be created by a project, as well as the activities necessary for their completion."},{"key":"B","text":"It manages the activity path that requires the longest time through the entire project."},{"key":"C","text":"It manages the events that may be advantageous or disadvantageous for the results of the project."},{"key":"D","text":"It coordinates the stakeholders of the implementation and results of the project."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"Project scope management determines what work and deliverables are included in the project and controls changes to that boundary. It covers both the product or service to be produced and the work required to produce it. Defining and managing deliverables and the necessary activities describes scope management."},{"id":52,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the water fall model known as one of software development models?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a technique in object-oriented development for making improvements through trial and error by repeatedly going back and forth between design and programming."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a technique for making improvements by repeating the development process for each subsystem while responding to requests from users."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a technique that divides the processes of system development into stages, and based upon the output of previous processes, performs later processes in order."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a technique that creates a prototype at an early stage of system development, and defines requirements and specifications with input from user comments."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"The waterfall model divides development into ordered stages such as requirements, design, implementation, testing, and installation. Each later stage uses approved outputs from earlier stages, with the main flow proceeding sequentially. Ordered stages based on the outputs of preceding stages describe the waterfall model."},{"id":53,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate metrics for program quality in a software development project?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Budget at planning"},{"key":"B","text":"Return on investment"},{"key":"C","text":"Delivery date"},{"key":"D","text":"Number of identified bugs"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"A program-quality metric measures an attribute or observed result of the software itself. The number of identified bugs is directly related to defects in the program, although it should be interpreted together with size, test coverage, severity, and test effort. The number of identified bugs is a metric related to program quality."},{"id":54,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"When the outsourced development project of a system has passed beyond its halfway mark, there is a request from the outsourcer for adding a function to the system. Which of the following is the most appropriate action of the project manager?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Accepting the request and securing the budget and staff members"},{"key":"B","text":"Declining the request by explaining that changes after halfway mark are generally not accepted"},{"key":"C","text":"Taking into account the impact on the cost and schedule, and following the procedure of change management"},{"key":"D","text":"Quickly updating the baseline of scope since only the project scope will be affected"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"A requested function addition is a proposed scope change. The project manager should analyze its effects on scope, cost, schedule, resources, quality, and risk, then submit it through the established change-control process before changing an approved baseline. Impact assessment followed by formal change management is the controlled response."},{"id":55,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of a master schedule in a system development project where processes from requirements definition to installation are performed?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A schedule that describes in detail the activities of one (1) week"},{"key":"B","text":"A schedule that describes the activities of one (1) day, the start and end time of the activities, and the persons in charge"},{"key":"C","text":"A schedule that describes in detail the activities of the main processes"},{"key":"D","text":"A schedule that aggregates the main deliverables and activities of the entire project"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"A master schedule presents the high-level timeline for the whole project. It summarizes major deliverables, phases, milestones, and activities so that overall progress and dependencies can be understood. An aggregate view of the entire project's main deliverables and activities is a master schedule."},{"id":56,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning WBS created in a project?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A WBS defines the details of activities to be implemented in a project and the deliverables, and can therefore be used as a basis for estimating the number of person-days."},{"key":"B","text":"Activities outside the scope of the project are also examined and included in the WBS."},{"key":"C","text":"The WBS breaks down the deliverables and the details of activities up to the same hierarchy in all projects."},{"key":"D","text":"When a project member performs similar activities within the scope, the activities need not be described in the WBS."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"A Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) decomposes the project's deliverables and work into manageable components. Those components support estimates of effort, duration, cost, responsibility, and scheduling. Detailed project work and deliverables in the WBS provide a basis for estimating person-days."},{"id":57,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Company A orders the development of a system to Company B and starts a system development project. Among (i) through (iv) below who are concerned with the project, which of the following lists all and only the stakeholders of the project?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(i), (ii), (iv)"},{"key":"B","text":"(i), (ii), (iii), (iv)"},{"key":"C","text":"(ii), (iii), (iv)"},{"key":"D","text":"(ii), (iv)"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"A stakeholder is any person, group, or organization that can affect the project, is affected by it, or perceives itself to be affected. This includes sponsor-side leaders and users as well as supplier-side management and supporting partners. All four groups can affect or be affected by the project and are stakeholders."},{"id":58,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the IT service management activity?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It defines the maturity level of a process in a system development organization on a level of one (1) to five (5), and supports improvement."},{"key":"B","text":"It defines roles and responsibilities and creates a procurement plan for staff members in order to complete a system development project."},{"key":"C","text":"It defines an index concerning system availability, acquires the availability record, and performs planning, measurements, and improvement in order to achieve an objective."},{"key":"D","text":"It clarifies the deliverables that are required for a new system to be developed and the activities that are required for the creation of the deliverables."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"IT service management includes availability management: agreeing availability targets, measuring actual availability, analyzing results, and planning improvements so that service objectives are met. Setting, measuring, and improving a system-availability objective is an IT service management activity."},{"id":59,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following activities aims at the maintenance and improvement of the service level through monitoring and reviewing the service status in order to implement the terms of agreement of an SLA?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"CSR"},{"key":"B","text":"ERP"},{"key":"C","text":"SLM"},{"key":"D","text":"SWOT"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"Service Level Management (SLM) manages agreed service targets throughout their life cycle. It monitors and reviews actual service performance against an SLA and drives actions that maintain or improve the service level. SLM is the activity that monitors and improves service levels to fulfill an SLA."},{"id":60,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate measure of facility management that maintains and protects facilities and equipment of information systems?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Reviewing the fuel replenishment plan in order to maintain the appropriate duration that power can be generated with a private power generation system"},{"key":"B","text":"Introducing asset management software in order to manage all the company’s software centrally"},{"key":"C","text":"Standardizing how to set a screen saver in order to prevent unauthorized use of the PCs"},{"key":"D","text":"Reviewing the network firewall settings in order to enhance the prevention of unauthorized network access to the information systems"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"Facility management protects the physical environment and infrastructure that support information systems, including buildings, electrical power, cooling, fire protection, and backup generation. Maintaining sufficient generator fuel directly supports continued facility operation. Reviewing backup-generator fuel replenishment protects the power facility needed by the information systems."},{"id":61,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate example concerning a chatbot that uses AI?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By connecting everything over the Internet, the switch of the air conditioner in one’s house can be turned on by a smart device from the outside of the house."},{"key":"B","text":"By recognizing and learning a large number of images of various animals, a computer can differentiate between the images of a dog and a cat."},{"key":"C","text":"If questions on how to use a product are entered, a person who has detailed knowledge submits a reply or advise."},{"key":"D","text":"If a user enters the desired functions of a product on a sales site of products, the computer introduces recommended products in an interactive manner."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"A chatbot conducts a text or voice conversation with a user and automatically returns responses or guides the interaction. An interactive product recommendation dialogue is therefore a chatbot use case. The computer asks about needs and interactively recommends products, which is a chatbot-style service."},{"id":62,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In order to improve the value of an IT service to be provided, it is necessary to consider the balance of three (3) items, namely the offer price of the service, the functions of the service, that is, what the service can offer, and a guarantee of the service with maintained availability. Which of the following is a description that corresponds to guarantee of the service of an instant messenger?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The service is usable for 24 hours a day, 365 days a year."},{"key":"B","text":"The service is linkable with other software such as games."},{"key":"C","text":"The service is usable for free."},{"key":"D","text":"The service is usable with icons created by one’s own self rather than characters."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"A service guarantee describes assurance that the service will be available, reliable, secure, or sufficiently capable when needed. Around-the-clock availability is a guarantee; features describe what the service does, and price describes its cost. Availability for 24 hours a day and 365 days a year is a service guarantee."},{"id":63,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description of the targets of a system audit?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Information systems used in private companies are not targeted."},{"key":"B","text":"Information systems that do not make use of the Internet are not targeted."},{"key":"C","text":"Activities other than accounting activities are not targeted."},{"key":"D","text":"Activities that do not make use of information systems are not targeted."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"A system audit evaluates controls related to information systems and the activities that use or support them. The scope is not limited by whether the organization is private, whether the system uses the Internet, or whether the activity is accounting. Activities that do not use or relate to information systems are outside the target described as a system audit."},{"id":64,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the term for the assignment of employees’ role that applies mutual checks among employees for the purpose of reducing the risk of misconduct or errors in work from the standpoint of internal control?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Delegation of authority"},{"key":"B","text":"Segregation of duties"},{"key":"C","text":"Monitoring"},{"key":"D","text":"Diversification of risk"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"Segregation of duties assigns incompatible parts of a process to different people. Requiring more than one person to initiate, approve, record, or review work creates mutual checks and reduces the chance that one person can make and conceal an error or fraud. Segregation of duties is the internal-control assignment that creates mutual checks."},{"id":65,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"The information system department implements the development and operation of the order entry system and the accounting system. The user of the order entry system is the sales department and the user of the accounting system is the accounting department. Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning internal control of financial reports?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Internal control is a matter of the accounting system, and therefore, the sales department does not participate in internal control, but the accounting department and the information system department do."},{"key":"B","text":"Internal control is a matter concerning accounting activities, and therefore, only the accounting department participates in internal control."},{"key":"C","text":"Internal control is a matter concerning activities that impact external reports such as financial statements, and therefore, the sales department, the accounting department and the information system department participate in internal control."},{"key":"D","text":"Internal control is a matter concerning activities that involve manual operation, and therefore, the information system department does not participate in internal control, but the sales department and the accounting department do."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"Internal control over financial reporting covers every process and system whose data can affect financial statements. Sales orders can feed revenue records, accounting processes the financial data, and information systems develop and operate the supporting systems, so all three departments participate. Sales, accounting, and information-system activities can all affect external financial reports."},{"id":66,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the scope that the CFO, one of the positions involved in corporate management, bears responsibility for?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Technology"},{"key":"B","text":"Finance"},{"key":"C","text":"Information"},{"key":"D","text":"Personnel"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"CFO stands for Chief Financial Officer. This executive is responsible for the organization's financial leadership, such as financial planning, reporting, funding, and management of financial risk. Finance is the CFO's responsibility."},{"id":67,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"There are activities A, B, and C that use machines X and Y, and it is required in each activity that the machines are used in the sequence of machine X, machine Y. When the use times of machines X and Y in each activity are as shown in the table below, which of the following is the sequence of the activities where the total time required to complete the three (3) activities becomes minimum? Here, machines X and Y can be used in parallel as shown in the figure below, but two (2) or more tasks cannot be performed simultaneously with any machine and the sequence of activities must be the same for both machines.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A → B → C"},{"key":"B","text":"A → C → B"},{"key":"C","text":"C → A → B"},{"key":"D","text":"C → B → A"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-27.png","explanation":"For sequence C → A → B, machine X finishes C, A, and B at minutes 6, 14, and 24. Machine Y processes C from 6 to 14, A from 14 to 24, and B from 24 to 29, so all work finishes in 29 minutes; evaluating the alternatives gives a longer completion time. C first uses its short 6-minute X time, A follows, and B with its short 5-minute Y time is last, producing the minimum 29 minutes."},{"id":68,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"The table below is a part of the ingredients table of a steamed meat dumplings lunch box. How many grams of meat is necessary to prepare 100 steamed meat dumplings lunch boxes? Here, the steamed meat dumplings lunch boxes do not contain any dish that uses meat other than the steamed meat dumplings, and there is no loss of ingredients in the preparing process.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"1,200"},{"key":"B","text":"3,000"},{"key":"C","text":"6,000"},{"key":"D","text":"30,000"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"One lunch box contains 5 dumplings, so 100 boxes require 500 dumplings. Each dumpling uses 20 g of stuffing, giving 10,000 g of stuffing, and meat is 60 g per 100 g of stuffing; therefore 10,000 × 0.60 = 6,000 g of meat. The chain 100 boxes × 5 dumplings × 20 g stuffing × 60/100 gives 6,000 g."},{"id":69,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following represents the “E” in ROE that is an index for the measurement of a company’s profitability?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Earnings"},{"key":"B","text":"Employee"},{"key":"C","text":"Enterprise"},{"key":"D","text":"Equity"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"ROE means Return on Equity. It measures profit relative to shareholders' equity, showing how effectively the company generates returns from the equity capital invested in it. The E in ROE stands for Equity."},{"id":70,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate terminology for referring to a method that uses AI, IoT, and other such IT for personnel-related work such as personnel evaluations and recruitment with aims including the improvement of a company’s personnel functions and achieving reform in working styles?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"e-Learning"},{"key":"B","text":"Fintech"},{"key":"C","text":"HR Tech"},{"key":"D","text":"Competency"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"HR Tech applies digital technologies such as AI, analytics, and IoT to human-resources work. It can support recruiting, evaluation, workforce management, employee experience, and work-style reform. HR Tech is technology applied to personnel and human-resources activities."},{"id":71,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is most appropriate as the person with responsibility for an information systems strategy that is created on the basis of a business strategy?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The CIO"},{"key":"B","text":"The head of the user department of mission-critical systems"},{"key":"C","text":"The project manager for system development"},{"key":"D","text":"The head of system planning"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"The Chief Information Officer (CIO) provides executive responsibility for aligning information systems and digital capabilities with business strategy. An information-systems strategy based on corporate strategy therefore falls under CIO leadership. The CIO is the executive responsible for information-systems strategy and its alignment with business strategy."},{"id":72,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an index that indicates the efficiency of capital utilization?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Ratio of operating profit to net sales"},{"key":"B","text":"Equity to total assets"},{"key":"C","text":"Total capital turnover"},{"key":"D","text":"Break-even point ratio"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"Total capital turnover compares sales with the total capital used to produce those sales. A higher turnover indicates that the company generates more sales per unit of capital, so it is an efficiency-of-capital-utilization index. Total capital turnover measures how efficiently capital is used to generate sales."},{"id":73,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an example of a Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A contract specifying the service content to be provided, which is agreed between the service provider and the customer before the provision of the IT service"},{"key":"B","text":"A contract specifying that the vendor of computer equipment bears the responsibility of transferring the property right, and that the buyer bears the responsibility of paying the charges"},{"key":"C","text":"A contract specifying the obligation of the outsourcer and outsourcee to maintain confidentiality of the secret information of a party that becomes known to the other party during system development"},{"key":"D","text":"A contract specifying that an outsourcee to whom the installation of a general-purpose software package has been outsourced performs the task at the outsourcee’s own discretion and responsibility, and receives payment upon the completion of the task"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"A Non-Disclosure Agreement imposes duties to protect confidential information received from another party and limits its use or disclosure. Such an agreement is common when organizations exchange sensitive information during outsourced development. Mutual obligations to keep development information confidential are the substance of an NDA."},{"id":74,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"From the viewpoint of corporate governance, which of the following is the most appropriate method of strengthening the functions of monitoring and supervising the decision-making process of the management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Installing a camera for monitoring the entry and exit of the president’s office"},{"key":"B","text":"Periodically requesting a private detective to investigate the conduct of the management"},{"key":"C","text":"Appointing some outside directors"},{"key":"D","text":"Employing law school graduates as members of the internal audit department"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"Outside directors can provide independent judgment and oversight that is less influenced by the company's internal management hierarchy. Their participation on the board strengthens monitoring of management decisions from a corporate-governance perspective. Outside directors strengthen independent monitoring and supervision of management."},{"id":75,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an international standard for environmental management systems developed by ISO?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ISO 9000"},{"key":"B","text":"ISO 14001"},{"key":"C","text":"ISO/IEC 20000"},{"key":"D","text":"ISO/IEC 27000"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"ISO 14001 specifies requirements for an environmental management system that an organization can use to manage environmental responsibilities systematically and improve environmental performance. ISO 14001 is the ISO standard for environmental management system requirements."},{"id":76,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following examples of the sending of e-mail is inappropriate from the standpoint of the protection of personal information?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In responding to an e-mail asking questions about a product, you placed the e-mail addresses of multiple customers in the “CC” field as you want these customers to read the response."},{"key":"B","text":"You created one (1) e-mail message for each of your top 10 customers with the largest amount of mail-order purchases, in order to inform each customer of a corresponding prize."},{"key":"C","text":"You sent an e-mail message with information on an alumni meeting, and addressed the message to the e-mail addresses of all members listed in the alumni association directory that is distributed to all members."},{"key":"D","text":"When you were arranging a special spring exhibition, you placed the e-mail addresses of selected members in the “BCC” field of an e-mail message and sent the message soliciting exhibits."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"Email addresses are personal information when they identify or relate to individuals. Putting multiple customers in Cc exposes every listed address to all recipients without the privacy protection that separate messages or Bcc would provide."},{"id":77,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate as an example of an enhancement activity for compliance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Expansion of a program to support the community service activities of employees"},{"key":"B","text":"Education for employees concerning laws and rules that must be followed"},{"key":"C","text":"Acquisition of another company’s business for swift business deployment"},{"key":"D","text":"Withdrawal from businesses where it is difficult to make profit"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"Compliance means that an organization and its employees follow applicable laws, regulations, contracts, and internal rules. Training makes employees aware of the requirements and how to act consistently with them. Teaching employees the laws and rules they must follow strengthens compliance."},{"id":78,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning an international organization for standardization?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ICANN is an international organization for standardization in the fields of industry, science, and technology."},{"key":"B","text":"IEC is an international organization for standardization in the field of e-commerce."},{"key":"C","text":"IEEE is an international organization for standardization in the field of accounting."},{"key":"D","text":"ITU is an international organization for standardization in the field of telecommunications."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"The International Telecommunication Union (ITU) develops international technical standards and coordinates matters in information and communication technologies and telecommunications. The other organizations listed have different fields or roles. ITU is an international standardization organization in telecommunications."},{"id":79,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In product portfolio management, where products and business to be analyzed are classified into cash cows, stars, dogs, and question marks, which of the following is the appropriate combination of indexes used in the vertical axis and horizontal axis?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"The growth-share matrix used in product portfolio management classifies businesses by market growth rate and relative market share. These two dimensions produce the categories stars, cash cows, question marks, and dogs. Market growth rate and market share are the two indexes used."},{"id":80,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In Company X, the experience and know-how of employees who have managed drainage treatment in the facility over a long period of time is documented and accumulated, and the accumulated experience and know-how is utilized on daily drainage treatment activities and design of new processing equipment. Which of the following is appropriate as a concept of this example?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ERP"},{"key":"B","text":"SFA"},{"key":"C","text":"Supply chain management"},{"key":"D","text":"Knowledge management"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"Knowledge management captures valuable experience and know-how that might otherwise remain only in individual employees' minds. It organizes, shares, and reuses that knowledge in ongoing work and future design or decision-making. Documenting, accumulating, and reusing employee know-how is knowledge management."},{"id":81,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following information is necessary for CRM?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Customer data and customer purchasing history"},{"key":"B","text":"Blueprint data"},{"key":"C","text":"Data of experts' knowledge"},{"key":"D","text":"Day and time of sales, shop, product sold, and quantity sold"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Customer Relationship Management (CRM) uses information about individual customers and their interactions with the company to improve sales, service, and retention. Customer profiles and purchasing history are core inputs for understanding needs and managing relationships. Customer data and purchasing history directly support CRM analysis and actions."},{"id":82,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a technique that analyzes the value of a product or service through the relationship between functionality and cost, and enhances that value through reduction in cost and increase in functionality and quality?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Supply chain management"},{"key":"B","text":"Knowledge management"},{"key":"C","text":"Value engineering"},{"key":"D","text":"Reverse engineering"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Value engineering examines the functions a product or service must provide in relation to the cost of providing them. It seeks greater value by preserving or improving necessary function and quality while reducing unnecessary cost. Analyzing function versus cost and improving that relationship is value engineering."},{"id":83,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of benchmarking used for corporate management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It refers to the promotion of continual improvement of business processes by applying the PDCA cycle."},{"key":"B","text":"It refers to the best case study for comparison and analysis when improvements are to be made."},{"key":"C","text":"It refers to the unique skills and technologies for securing superiority over competitors."},{"key":"D","text":"It refers to the measurement of the products and services of one’s company, and their comparison with other superior competitors."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Benchmarking measures an organization's products, services, or processes and compares them with strong performers or recognized best practices. The comparison reveals performance gaps and ideas for improvement. Measuring the company's offerings and comparing them with superior competitors describes benchmarking."},{"id":84,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"With the purpose of increasing the number of contracts concluded, salespersons in Company A’s sales department began an activity to make proposals for plans to customers. A key goal indicator (KGI) and key performance indicator (KPI) are to be set as indexes for achievement of sales activities. Which of the following is the most appropriate combination of KGI and KPI in this activity?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No. of contracts concludedSales amount"},{"key":"B","text":"No. of contracts concludedNo. of proposals"},{"key":"C","text":"No. of proposalsSales amount"},{"key":"D","text":"No. of proposalsNo. of contracts concluded"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"A KGI measures the final outcome the activity is intended to achieve, while a KPI measures an important activity or intermediate performance that contributes to that outcome. Here the goal is more concluded contracts, and making proposals is the sales activity expected to lead to them. Number of contracts is the goal outcome, and number of proposals is a leading activity indicator."},{"id":85,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description of a “patent portfolio” that is important for establishing the patent strategy?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a compilation of patents owned and filed by a company to analyze their contribution to business, the synergy among them, and the expected fields of their applications."},{"key":"B","text":"At the beginning of a technological innovation, patent applications tend to increase, but because of the emergence of dominant products in the market, there is a shift to process innovation, and patent applications decrease."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a matrix with the share of the products of one’s company and the growth rate of the market as the axes, showing the positioning of the company and its competitors in the market."},{"key":"D","text":"Multiple patent holders mutually grant their patent licenses."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"A patent portfolio is the organized set of patents and patent applications controlled by an organization. Reviewing it as a whole helps assess business contribution, coverage, gaps, synergies, and opportunities for future use or licensing. A compiled and strategically analyzed collection of owned and filed patents is a patent portfolio."},{"id":86,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the situation where an improvement can be expected by installing an MRP (Material Requirements Planning) system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Drawing information is managed using electronic files and hard copies, so the design change history cannot be accurately known."},{"key":"B","text":"Information concerning materials necessary for manufacturing and their required quantities is insufficient or incorrect, so production is adversely affected."},{"key":"C","text":"There are too many design change requests, so production efficiency does not increase."},{"key":"D","text":"High-mix, low-volume production is adopted, so the cost of installing production equipment is increasing."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"Material Requirements Planning (MRP) calculates what materials are needed, in what quantities, and when, based on production plans, bills of materials, inventory, and lead times. It directly addresses shortages or errors in material requirement information. MRP improves planning of required manufacturing materials and quantities."},{"id":87,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of a banner advertisement that is a form of Internet advertisement?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a website is being browsed, an advertisement from an advertiser is displayed in another new window."},{"key":"B","text":"When a web page is accessed from another page, a page with an advertisement is briefly shown before the accessed page is displayed."},{"key":"C","text":"When an advertisement image that is placed on part of a web page is clicked, an advertiser page is displayed."},{"key":"D","text":"When keywords are entered into a search site, an advertisement related to the keywords is displayed on the page showing the search results."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"A banner advertisement is a graphical advertising area embedded in part of a web page. Clicking the image or graphic normally opens the advertiser's landing page. A clickable advertisement image placed within a web page is a banner advertisement."},{"id":88,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"A company wishes to create digital files from paper documents and paper blueprints, and make these available company-wide. Which of the following is appropriate equipment to be used?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"GPS receiver"},{"key":"B","text":"Scanner"},{"key":"C","text":"Digitizer"},{"key":"D","text":"Plotter"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"A scanner captures the visible content of paper documents and drawings and converts it into digital image files. It is therefore suitable for digitizing an existing collection of paper documents and blueprints for company-wide access. A scanner converts paper pages and blueprints into digital images."},{"id":89,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of CAD?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a circuit that converts an analog signal into a digital signal."},{"key":"B","text":"It refers to the use of computers in the design of buildings and industrial products."},{"key":"C","text":"It is an imaging element that converts light to an electrical signal."},{"key":"D","text":"It refers to the creation of a single piece of content by combining characters, images, audio, and other data."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"CAD means Computer-Aided Design. CAD software supports creation, modification, analysis, and documentation of designs for buildings, machinery, electronic products, and other engineered objects. Using computers to design buildings and industrial products is CAD."},{"id":90,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate example of a use of a wearable device?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Using a PC or tablet computer, and receiving diagnosis from a doctor over a network"},{"key":"B","text":"Acquiring blood pressure, body temperature, and other such measurement data with a smartwatch, and detecting abnormalities at an early stage"},{"key":"C","text":"Managing and sharing the computerized data of patient records from multiple hospitals in a cloud service"},{"key":"D","text":"Installing a human presence sensor in a bed, and sending a notification if the sensor does not respond for a certain length of time"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"A wearable device is designed to be worn on the body and can continuously or conveniently collect data while the user goes about daily life. A smartwatch measuring vital signs is a direct wearable-device use. A smartwatch is wearable and can collect health measurements for early abnormality detection."},{"id":91,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"An EC site handles a wide range of user inquiries via chat with a mechanism where operators provide a response. It decides to use a new mechanism where software learns from the content of users’ past chats, infers an appropriate response from the flow of the conversation and provides an automatic response. Which of the following is the most appropriate technology that is used in the new mechanism?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI"},{"key":"B","text":"AR"},{"key":"C","text":"CRM"},{"key":"D","text":"ERP"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"The new mechanism learns patterns from previous conversations and infers responses from the current dialogue. Learning and inference from data are characteristic applications of artificial intelligence. AI supports learning from chat history and automatically generating or selecting an appropriate response."},{"id":92,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate term to express the initiatives that are implemented by a financial institution or other such institution in order to prevent acts where funds obtained illegally are disguised as being obtained by legitimate means?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Anti-money laundering (AML)"},{"key":"B","text":"Insider trading regulations"},{"key":"C","text":"Skimming"},{"key":"D","text":"Phishing"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"Money laundering attempts to conceal the criminal origin of funds and make them appear legitimate. Anti-money laundering programs use customer checks, transaction monitoring, reporting, and other controls to prevent and detect that activity. AML is the collective term for initiatives against disguising illegally obtained funds."},{"id":93,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning groupware?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is software that has an animation or audio function and is useful when making presentations effective by incorporating the output of spreadsheet software or database software."},{"key":"B","text":"It is software that has functions, such as setting print layout or changing and editing texts, and is used for creating documents."},{"key":"C","text":"It is software that has functions, such as communication via e-mail and electronic bulletin boards, data sharing, and schedule management, and supports collaborative work."},{"key":"D","text":"It is software that is used to enter data into cells of a worksheet, create tables, and tabulate data."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"Groupware provides shared tools that help people coordinate and work together. Typical functions include messaging, discussion boards, shared files, calendars, scheduling, and collaborative workflows. Communication, information sharing, and schedule management are core groupware functions."},{"id":94,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a modeling technique that is used for analyzing business operations and system from the viewpoint of the flow of data which is exchanged between processes?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"BPR"},{"key":"B","text":"DFD"},{"key":"C","text":"MRP"},{"key":"D","text":"WBS"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"A Data Flow Diagram (DFD) models how data moves among external entities, processes, and data stores. It is used to analyze business operations or systems from the viewpoint of data inputs, transformations, storage, and outputs. DFD is the modeling technique centered on data exchanged between processes."},{"id":95,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Training on how to use a sales forecast system is planned for the persons in charge of business across the country. Which of the following is a merit that is obtained by using e-learning in training?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The person in charge of business can be directly lectured about the system from the person in charge of design, and raise questions then and there."},{"key":"B","text":"The person in charge of business can use his/her own free time and undergo training at any suitable time."},{"key":"C","text":"Several persons in charge of business can participate together and exchange their opinions on how to use the system."},{"key":"D","text":"The persons in charge of business can be asked to assemble together in a room and training can be given simultaneously."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"E-learning can deliver the same training materials over a network without requiring every learner to travel to one classroom at one time. In an asynchronous course, geographically distributed learners can study when their own schedules permit. Flexible timing is a major advantage of e-learning for distributed learners."},{"id":96,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Attempts are being made to streamline the functions and services of cities and regions and make them more advanced with the use of ICT in order to solve regional problems, and vitalize regions. Which of the following is the most appropriate term to describe such a solution for community development?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Capacity"},{"key":"B","text":"Smart city"},{"key":"C","text":"Diversity"},{"key":"D","text":"University"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"A smart city uses ICT, connected data, and digital services to improve urban functions and address community issues such as transport, energy, safety, health, and public administration. The objective is a more effective, sustainable, and attractive region. ICT-enabled improvement and advancement of city and regional services describes a smart city."},{"id":97,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"In system development, which of the following is a process that clarifies the business functions to be newly constructed or reconstructed, and on the basis of the business functions, specifies the scope of computerization and the functions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"External design"},{"key":"B","text":"Internal design"},{"key":"C","text":"Programming"},{"key":"D","text":"Requirements definition"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"Requirements definition determines what business functions the new or changed system must support, what is included in the computerization scope, and what functions and constraints the system must satisfy. Design and programming follow after those needs are clarified. Clarifying business functions, system scope, and required functions is requirements definition."},{"id":98,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description of IoT?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a learning mechanism in artificial intelligence."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a mechanism where devices or control units equipped with a sensor connect to the Internet and exchange a variety of information via the Internet."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a group of functions and procedures that are made public in order to enable some of the features of a piece of software to be used by other programs."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a tool that uses a software robot to streamline routine work."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"The Internet of Things (IoT) connects physical devices equipped with sensors, actuators, or control units to networks. The devices collect, exchange, and sometimes act on information through Internet-based services. Internet-connected devices and control units exchanging sensed information describe IoT."},{"id":99,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate word to indicate the use of IoT, AI, and other IT in order to strategically overhaul a business model and produce new added value?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Digital signage"},{"key":"B","text":"Digital divide"},{"key":"C","text":"Digital transformation"},{"key":"D","text":"Digital native"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"Digital transformation uses digital technologies and data to change business models, processes, customer value, and sometimes organizational culture. It goes beyond simply digitizing an existing task by pursuing strategic change and new value. Strategic business-model reform and new value creation through IoT, AI, and other IT is digital transformation."},{"id":100,"session":"2024S","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of an RFP that is created by a company, government organization, or other such organization that is planning the introduction of a new system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a document created for collecting information from vendors and determining a system’s technical issues and feasibility."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a definition of matters such as the performance requirements for a new system by the vendor and the ordering party."},{"key":"C","text":"It sets out the agreed matters concerning the level of service quality between the vendor and the ordering party."},{"key":"D","text":"It provides vendors with the objective of introduction and a functional overview of the system, and solicit a bid."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-38.png","explanation":"A Request for Proposal (RFP) explains the buyer's objectives, needs, scope, and functional overview and asks vendors to submit proposed solutions and bids. The proposals can then be evaluated as part of vendor and solution selection. Giving vendors the introduction objective and functional overview and soliciting bids describes an RFP."}];